
---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy Policy for the Clockwork Otter Foundry website."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[var(--content-max-width)] px-6 py-24">
    <div class="max-w-[var(--reading-max-width)]">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Effective date: October 14, 2026
      </p>

      <p class="mt-6 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Clockwork Otter Foundry LLC, a Florida limited liability
        company, respects the privacy of visitors to this website.
        We have intentionally designed this website to collect
        as little personal information as reasonably possible.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Information We Collect</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Clockwork Otter Foundry does not currently provide user
        accounts, login functionality, contact forms, analytics
        services, advertising trackers, or behavioral profiling
        on this website.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We do not intentionally collect personal information
        directly from visitors simply for browsing the website.
        Our hosting provider may process technical information
        as described below.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        If you choose to contact us by email, we receive the
        information you voluntarily include in that communication,
        such as your email address, name if provided, message
        content, and any other information you choose to send.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Email Communications</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Email links on this website open your own email application
        or service. The website does not submit your message
        through a Clockwork Otter Foundry web form.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Information you send by email is used to read, respond to,
        and manage your inquiry and for reasonable business
        recordkeeping related to that correspondence.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We do not automatically enroll individuals who contact
        us in marketing communications.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Cookies and Analytics</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Clockwork Otter Foundry does not currently use analytics
        services, advertising technologies, behavioral tracking,
        or tracking cookies on this website.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We may revise these practices in the future. Any material
        changes involving cookies, analytics, or tracking will
        be reflected in this Privacy Policy, and consent will
        be obtained where required by applicable law.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Hosting and Technical Information</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        This website is hosted using GitHub Pages, a service
        provided by GitHub.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        GitHub may process routine technical information when
        visitors access the website to deliver, operate, maintain,
        and secure its services. GitHub states that visitor IP
        addresses for GitHub Pages websites are logged and
        stored for security purposes.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        GitHub's privacy practices may also cover information
        relating to devices, sessions, and requests. This
        processing is subject to GitHub's applicable privacy
        terms and practices.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Clockwork Otter Foundry does not use GitHub Pages
        visitor information for its own advertising or
        behavioral analytics.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Additional information about GitHub's privacy practices
        is available in the
        <a
          href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="font-medium underline"
        >
          GitHub Privacy Statement
        </a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Third-Party Services and Links</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        This website may contain links to third-party websites,
        software repositories, marketplaces, and other services,
        including GitHub and Amazon.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        When you follow a third-party link, that service's
        own terms and privacy practices apply. Clockwork Otter
        Foundry does not control the information collected
        directly by those third-party websites.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Purchases of books or other products through third-party
        marketplaces are processed by the applicable marketplace,
        not through this website.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Website fonts are served locally rather than requested
        from an external font service, provided the website
        continues to use its current configuration.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">How We Use Information</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        When you voluntarily provide personal information
        by contacting us, we use it as reasonably necessary to:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        <li>respond to your inquiry;</li>
        <li>communicate about the subject of your message;</li>
        <li>maintain appropriate business records;</li>
        <li>protect the security of our communications; and</li>
        <li>comply with applicable legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We do not sell personal information or use information
        submitted through ordinary email correspondence for
        behavioral advertising.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Where applicable data-protection law requires a legal
        basis for processing personal information, the basis
        depends on the circumstances and may include taking
        steps at your request, complying with legal obligations,
        or our legitimate interests in operating the business,
        maintaining security, and responding to correspondence.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Data Minimization and Retention</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We retain personal information only for as long as
        reasonably necessary for the purposes for which it
        was received, including responding to correspondence,
        maintaining appropriate business records, resolving
        disputes, protecting legal rights, and complying
        with applicable legal obligations.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Information that is no longer reasonably needed
        will be deleted or otherwise handled in accordance
        with applicable requirements.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">International Processing</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Clockwork Otter Foundry LLC is based in Florida,
        United States. The website and services used to
        operate the business may involve infrastructure
        located in different countries.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        As a result, technical information and communications
        may be processed outside the country in which a
        visitor resides.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Where applicable law requires specific safeguards
        for international transfers of personal information,
        we will address those requirements in connection
        with the services and processing activities involved.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Privacy Rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Depending on your location and applicable law, you
        may have rights concerning personal information
        about you, including rights to request access,
        correction, deletion, restriction, portability,
        or objection to certain processing.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        You may submit privacy-related requests by emailing
        <a
          href="mailto:info@clockworkotterfoundry.com"
          class="font-medium underline"
        >
          info@clockworkotterfoundry.com
        </a>.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We will review and respond to requests in accordance
        with applicable law. We may need to verify your
        identity before fulfilling certain requests.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Where applicable, individuals may also have the
        right to lodge a complaint with the relevant
        data-protection authority.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Children's Privacy</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        This website is a general informational website
        and is not directed specifically to children.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Clockwork Otter Foundry does not knowingly use
        this website to solicit personal information
        from children.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Security</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We take reasonable steps appropriate to the nature
        of this website and the limited information we
        receive to protect information under our control.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        However, no internet transmission, email system,
        or storage system can be guaranteed to be
        completely secure.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        We may update this Privacy Policy when our website,
        business practices, services, or applicable legal
        requirements change.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        When this policy is materially updated, the effective
        date at the top of this page will be updated.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-12">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        For questions about this Privacy Policy or
        privacy-related requests, please contact:
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        <strong>Clockwork Otter Foundry LLC</strong>
        <span class="block">
          12652 Pine Marsh Way
        </span>
        <span class="block">
          Jacksonville, FL 32226
        </span>
        <span class="block">
          United States
        </span>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        <a
          href="mailto:info@clockworkotterfoundry.com"
          class="font-medium underline"
        >
          info@clockworkotterfoundry.com
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
